%N A398460 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} H(k) * AH(k,2) / k^2, where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number, and AH(k,2) = A119682(k)/A334580(k) is the k-th alternating harmonic (or skew-harmonic) number of order 2.
%H A398460 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.46, p. 439, eq. (4.147), section 5.46, p. 466, section 6.46, pp. 715-723.
